    "q-114240": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114240",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{x}-x-1}=$",
      "worked_solution": "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{e}^{x}-x-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[{x}^{2}]^{′}}{[{e}^{x}-x-1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{{e}^{x}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x-1+{e}^{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{{e}^{x}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[2x]^{′}}{[{e}^{x}-1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{e}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-114240-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-1",
              "html": " <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"37\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-114240-b",
